Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns, what they are good for, and typical conditions  
• `state` : 2‑letter (sometimes mixed‑case) state abbreviation – use to count / group events by state; filter out NULLs.  
• `event_begin_time` : when the event started – not strictly needed because every table already represents one calendar year, but could still be used if you UNION several years that live in the same table.  
• `event_id` : unique weather–event id – only needed if you want to do a DISTINCT count instead of the default COUNT(*).  
• `event_type`, `cz_type`, … : not required for this task but can be added to extra filters (e.g. hail only).  

Basic condition you will see in most queries  
WHERE state IS NOT NULL

